James was developing a Shiny app and encountered layout issues when using `page_navbar` with `bootstrapPage`, resulting in vertical column arrangement. I explained that `page_navbar` is compatible with Bootstrap 4, recommending he switch to `fluidPage`, which works well with the newer layout systems. I provided a structured example using `fluidRow` and `column` to ensure proper horizontal alignment. He then asked how to incorporate a `sidebarPanel` and main content area within a `fluidPage`. I confirmed that it is suitable and shared an example using `sidebarLayout`, consisting of `sidebarPanel` for inputs and `mainPanel` for outputs. I offered guidance on using the layout effectively, highlighting its adaptability and responsiveness.
